    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Security at Every Stage of the Software Lifecycle
        </h2>

        <p>
            As organizations become more dependent on digital systems, protecting
            business information and maintaining reliable operations become
            increasingly important. Security weaknesses can expose sensitive
            data, interrupt services, and undermine customer trust.
        </p>

        <p>
            Security should be considered from the earliest stages of software
            design rather than added only after implementation. Secure
            architecture, appropriate authentication, access controls, input
            validation, dependency management, and careful handling of sensitive
            information help reduce common application risks.
        </p>

        <p>
            OnnaSoft incorporates security considerations into technology
            planning and development according to each project's requirements.
            Relevant practices may include code reviews, automated security
            checks, secure configuration, secrets management, vulnerability
            assessment, and controlled deployment workflows.
        </p>

        <p>
            Protecting an application also requires ongoing attention. Regular
            updates, monitoring, backup procedures, and incident response
            planning help organizations maintain resilience as their systems
            and operational requirements change.
        </p>
    </section>

